--- Web source parity (features/dashboard/widgets/ChargeSessionChartWidget.tsx) ---
- Data: useVehicles + useQuery('/charging?vehicle_id=&limit=10') -> bound natively via the shared
  P1/S8 ChargingStore.sessionsPaginated(limit:10) + VehiclesStore (first-vehicle fallback) through
  StateHolderModel -> LoadableState (no HTTP in the view).
- classifyChargerType(): reproduced exactly (supercharger/tesla -> supercharger; non-empty & != "<invalid>"
  -> dc; else home). CHARGER_COLORS parity via design tokens (home->success #10b981, sc->danger #ef4444,
  dc->warning #f59e0b).
- Energy hardcoded to kWh (Wh/1000) and reversed series, matching the web useMemo pipeline.
- States reproduced: loading (skeleton), content (bar chart + legend + Total/Avg/Sessions), empty
  ("No charge sessions yet"), error (retry), stale (chip), offline (chip + cached). Compact size -> summary only.
- i18n: translation.widget.chargeSessionChart.{title,total,avg,sessions,empty} (pre-existing, exact EN values)
  + added .type.{home,supercharger,dc} + .stale; chrome reuses translation.common.{refresh,retry,loading,offline}
  + translation.kWh + translation.Error. No hardcoded English in native code.
- Accessibility: VoiceOver labels/values on every bar, legend item, chip, summary metric; Dynamic Type via
  Font.TS tokens; reduce-motion honored on chart animation.
- Telemetry: emits view.opened with surface slug "ChargeSessionChartWidget" via the DashboardWidgetTelemetry
  seam (ScreenViewWidgetTelemetry forwards to the shared-core P1/S11 Telemetry.ScreenView taxonomy).
- Registry: descriptor id "charge-session-chart", category "charging", default 2x4, min 1x2, max 4x40
  (parity with web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/registry/charging.ts), asserted by a unit test.

